  "units": {
    "ts": "sea-level reference-season temperature, Celsius",
    "tw": "sea-level opposite-reference-season temperature, Celsius",
    "ps": "reference half-year precipitation, mm",
    "pw": "opposite half-year precipitation, mm",
    "ls": "reference-season positive lapse, Celsius/metre",
    "lw": "opposite-season positive lapse, Celsius/metre",
    "altitudes": "mean physical land altitude, metres",
    "sand": "unit fraction; fixed across all climates to isolate the climate axis"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The repository has 30 terrestrial Koppen classes plus ocean ID 0, grouped here into 15 review families. Render v2 evaluates continuous climate and legacy ecology rather than selecting a class palette.",
    "expectedCode is the production Koppen classification at elevation zero with default thresholds, before the altitude lapse. Reclassify at every actual altitude instead of relabelling an alpine EF patch Af.",
    "All ts/tw pairs designate northern warm/cold reference seasons. Render v2 date 0.5 uses ts, date 0 uses tw. Swapping both seasons and precipitation together is the separate southern-hemisphere control.",
    "The default physical lapse is (4.5 + 4.8*(1-clamp(halfYearRain/1000,0,1)))/1000 Celsius/metre, independently for each reference season. Do not substitute an arbitrary fixed 0.0065.",
    "A visible plate must span exactly 40000 metres in both physical axes. Overview metres/pixel is 40000/renderedPlatePixels; close insets must state their own smaller extent.",
    "At overview footprints above 6m/pixel, Render v2 inherits the legacy open ground; at above 32m/pixel explicit crown detail is unresolved. Inspect ecology buffers or clearly labelled close insets to validate tree exclusion.",
    "Altitude-only rows keep sea-level temperatures and precipitation fixed. Effective displayed climate and tree/snow gates must use ts-ls*max(height,0), tw-lw*max(height,0)."
  ],
  "expectedGates": {
    "warmGrowth": "Legacy macro woods begin at local hottest-season 5.5C, reach their thermal range by 13.5C; explicit crown thermal range is 5..8.5C and is further gated by the legacy eligibility and perennial snow. Topographic jitter slightly moves the transition.",
    "grass": "Legacy herbs need warm-season 0..7C and humidity 0.2..0.85; current green tone depends on current temperature 3..12C and current humidity 0.5..1.4. Cold/dry grass is not necessarily green.",
    "aridity": "Koppen aridity uses max(0,20*meanTemperature + seasonalAddition), with additions 280/140/0mm for warm-rain fractions >=0.7 / intermediate / <=0.3. Desert is below half the aridity threshold, steppe below the full threshold. Render material humidity uses its separate continuous max(120,20*meanTemperature+280) denominator.",
    "snow": "Render v2 continuous cold retention spans current temperature +2..-5C, humidity potential 0.12..0.7 and slope shedding 0.45..1.25. Cold wet flat ground may reach full snow; steep slopes expose rock. EF with rain and a frozen river must have no woody candidates.",
    "polar": "ET is hottest season 0<=T<10C, EF is hottest season T<0C; both override aridity classification. An ET case with hottest season 6C can sit near the implemented sparse woody threshold, so do not assert zero trees for all ET.",
    "water": "Ocean is a separate hydrology/elevation state, not a forced terrestrial Koppen case. Complement these rows with open sea/pack/icebergs, warm/frozen lakes and rivers, plus authoritative dry below-sea-level basins.",
    "visual": "Use the same 40km terrain, seed, camera, lighting, sand and seasonal dates across climate rows. Require readable lit/shadowed relief under snow and vegetation, no synthetic red contour halos, no land texture crossing authoritative water, and broad color/coverage continuity between DEM resolutions and latitudes."
  },
